-- examples/checks/agg-member-derivs-state-check.rofl — agg_member_derivs_state:
-- the cells of agg-member-derivs.rofl as sealed, no fact retracted. Each member
-- lists its canonical derivation first and every other one after it as `alt`,
-- in text order: sale 2 of a is counted four ways through md_ok (the canonical
-- is the text-least, w, though z rests on a level more) and three through
-- md_chan, sale 3 of b two ways, and sales 1 and 4 one way each, with no `alt`. The ids are
-- the members' own: they do not depend on how many derivations a member has.
-- expect-row: cell $cell(r71cb3651,2,0,$cons(a,$nil)) median = 5 h=1 tick=0 sealed=[md_sale@0, md_chan@0] alg=holistic use=recompute
-- expect-row: mem $cell(r71cb3651,2,0,$cons(a,$nil)) #1 id=3d01e0788910195b (10,1) h=1 [fact:md_chan[main](1,x); fact:md_sale[main](1,a,10)]
-- expect-row: mem $cell(r71cb3651,2,0,$cons(a,$nil)) #2 id=a58a6e49fc95c4d2 (5,2) h=1 [fact:md_chan[main](2,w); fact:md_sale[main](2,a,5)] alt [fact:md_chan[main](2,x); fact:md_sale[main](2,a,5)] alt [fact:md_chan[main](2,y); fact:md_sale[main](2,a,5)]
-- expect-row: cell $cell(r71cb3651,2,0,$cons(b,$nil)) median = 7 h=1 tick=0 sealed=[md_sale@0, md_chan@0] alg=holistic use=recompute
-- expect-row: mem $cell(r71cb3651,2,0,$cons(b,$nil)) #1 id=b793cd9186439be8 (7,3) h=1 [fact:md_chan[main](3,x); fact:md_sale[main](3,b,7)] alt [fact:md_chan[main](3,y); fact:md_sale[main](3,b,7)]
-- expect-row: mem $cell(r71cb3651,2,0,$cons(b,$nil)) #2 id=b797359186468277 (7,4) h=1 [fact:md_chan[main](4,x); fact:md_sale[main](4,b,7)]
